Package: patliR
Type: Package
Title: Reproducible Network Pharmacology Analysis for Natural Product Extracts
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Edgard Uriel", family = "López Chablé",
    email = "uriel.chable18@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A field-to-report pipeline for network pharmacology analysis of
    natural product extracts and compound mixtures. Provides functions to
    import and validate compound identity from PubChem CIDs or SMILES,
    integrate physicochemical (ADME) properties and structural toxicity
    alerts, import or predict protein targets, build and analyze
    compound-target-pathway networks (centrality, modular robustness,
    network proximity to disease modules, synergy), audit database bias in
    network pharmacology results, and generate transparent, fully-logged
    reports. The pipeline is built around an immutable S4 project object:
    every step is a pure transformation (input project -> output project),
    and every intermediate result is written to a plain CSV file that acts
    as the durable, portable source of truth, independent of any R-specific
    binary format.
